@base = http://localhost:8000
@memberToken = paste_member_token_here
@adminToken = paste_admin_token_here

### Health / API info
GET {{base}}/

### Public books
GET {{base}}/api/books

### Login as member
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "member@books.test",
  "password": "password"
}

### Login as admin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@books.test",
  "password": "password"
}

### Current user
GET {{base}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}

### Create book as member
POST {{base}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Refactoring",
  "author": "Martin Fowler",
  "year": 2018,
  "genre": "Software Engineering"
}

### Chapter 12 validation test: future year should return 400
POST {{base}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Future Book",
  "author": "X",
  "year": 9999
}

### Chapter 12 XSS-safe output test
POST {{base}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "<script>alert('hi')</script>",
  "author": "X",
  "year": 2024
}

### Chapter 12 IDOR test: member tries to update admin-owned book 1, expect 403
PUT {{base}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Hijacked"
}

### Chapter 12 admin update: expect 200
PUT {{base}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clean Code Updated"
}

### Chapter 12 rate limit: run 6 times with wrong password; 6th should be 429
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@books.test",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### Chapter 12 CORS allowed origin preflight
OPTIONS {{base}}/api/books
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Authorization, Content-Type

### Chapter 12 CORS attacker origin preflight
OPTIONS {{base}}/api/books
Origin: http://attacker.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Authorization, Content-Type
